    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I reproduced this on latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nSelecting a file to open in file picker doesn't work. Instead it triggers mini.jump2d\n\n### Reproduction\n\nSteps to repro:\n1. After setup, run NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-minimax nvim\n2. <Space> e \n3. d or f\n4. navigate to a file using hjkl\n5. select a file and <CR>\n\nExpectation:\nI was expecting it will open the selected file in buffer\n\nWhat happens:\nall file names shows as garbage and then I see a (mini.jump2d) Enter encoding symbol to advanced jump\n\nI think it seems conflicting keymaps or something.",
